+# `xlmroberta`: BGE-M3 and its reranker
+
+`arch/xlmroberta` is an embedding program like `nomicbert`: a pooled output, no sampler, no KV
+cache, one step an input. One card (`tp: 1`).
+
+```
+text      24 layers, hidden 1024, ffn 4096, vocab 250002, 16 heads of 64, type vocab 1
+          trained to 8194 positions, the first two of them padding_idx's
+          post-norm block: a = out(attn(Wqkv h + b)) + b_out; h = LN1(h + a)
+          dense MLP, fc2(gelu(fc1 h + b1)) + b2, exact gelu; h = LN2(h + m)
+          query, key and value fused [q|k|v] at convert time, non-causal, scale 0.125
+          embeddings: word + position (rows from 2 on) + token_type, then LayerNorm
+```
+
+The pooled row is chosen by the checkpoint. `XLMRobertaModel` returns the `<s>` row, 1024 wide.
+With `--set sparse_linear=1` and BGE-M3's `sparse_linear.pt` beside the checkpoint renamed
+`sparse_linear.pth`, the row continues with the sparse logit of each position, `max-model-len`
+of them, zero past the input: 1024 + 512 wide at `max-model-len: 512`. The logits are before
+BGE-M3's relu, and the client takes the positive ones and the maximum per token id, so it
+tokenises the input and sends the ids. `XLMRobertaForSequenceClassification` returns
+`out_proj(tanh(dense(<s>)))`, one f32 logit; `out_proj` runs in f32 because a bf16 logit near 8
+is rounded to a multiple of 1/16.
+
+Neither row is a unit vector, so a request sets `"normalize": false` on `/v1/embeddings`. The
+reranker reads a pair as the client builds it, `<s> query </s></s> document </s>`; `/rerank`
+formats Nemotron's pairs only.
+
+```sh
+rad-convert <bge-m3 dir> --recipe data/recipes/bge-m3-bf16.recipe --set sparse_linear=1 \
+    -o bge-m3-bf16.rad
+rad-convert <bge-reranker-v2-m3 dir> --recipe data/recipes/bge-reranker-v2-m3-bf16.recipe \
+    -o bge-reranker-v2-m3-bf16.rad
+```
+
+BGE-M3 ships only `pytorch_model.bin`, which rad-convert passes over, so its directory needs the
+same tensors as `model.safetensors`.
+
+---
